# Exclude patterns for the workstation backup (Kopia, gitignore-style syntax).
#
# Applied by install-backup.ps1 as POLICY rules (kopia policy set --add-ignore), not by
# dropping .kopiaignore files into the user's tree -- the source directories are git repos
# and we do not want a stray ignore file showing up as untracked in every one of them.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are skipped by the installer.
#
# Three reasons a path appears here. Keep them straight, because they have different fixes:
#   REBUILDABLE - a cache or a downloadable artifact. Excluding it costs nothing.
#   UNSAFE      - a file that cannot be captured consistently by a file-level backup.
#   SECRET      - a live credential we deliberately refuse to ship to a third-party host.
#
# Measured on DESKTOP1, 2026-09-06: these patterns take ~54 GB raw down to ~2.6 GB.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# UNSAFE -- virtual disk images
#
# VSS snapshots the host NTFS volume. It does NOT quiesce the ext4 filesystem inside a
# VHDX, so what gets captured is a byte copy of a live disk mid-write with a torn journal.
# It may mount on restore; it may not; you find out at the worst moment. WSL distros belong
# in `wsl --export` tarballs (quiesced, and a fine Kopia target). Docker images come from
# registries, and named volumes from `docker run --rm -v <vol>:/v alpine tar -cf - /v`.
# Measured: 5.23 GB in three files.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
AppData/Local/wsl/
AppData/Local/Docker/wsl/
AppData/Local/Docker/log/
*.vhdx
*.vhd
*.vmdk

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRET -- live credentials, deliberately not backed up
#
# Every item here is rotatable in minutes, so excluding it loses nothing recoverable while
# removing a standing risk: an encrypted repository on someone else's disk that decrypts to
# production access if the passphrase ever leaks.
#
# .claude/projects is on this list for a reason discovered rather than assumed: on
# 2026-09-06 two separate agent transcripts in that directory were found to contain live
# API keys in plaintext, written there by ordinary tool output. Conversation transcripts
# accumulate secrets as a matter of course. It is also 764 MB and grows without bound.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.doppler/
.ssh/
.codex/auth.json
.hi_token
.hi_url
.claude/projects/
.chrome-debug-*/

# NOTE on the line above: excluding .claude/projects/ also excludes the memory/ directory
# inside each project slug -- which is Claude's accumulated "don't re-do this" record, is
# not in git, and per scripts/newpc/README.md cannot be reinstalled. That would be the
# worst possible thing to lose here. backup-run.ps1 therefore adds every
# .claude/projects/*/memory directory back as its OWN snapshot source; ignore rules apply
# while traversing down from a source root, so a source inside an ignored path is still
# captured. If you edit either half of this, edit both.

