# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REBUILDABLE -- Chromium-family caches (Chrome, Edge, and every Electron app)
#
# What is KEPT, per profile: Login Data, Login Data For Account, Web Data, Cookies,
# Preferences, Secure Preferences, Bookmarks, History, Favicons, Local Extension Settings,
# Extension State, Storage/ext, and User Data/Local State.
#
# Be aware of what keeping them actually buys. Those files are DPAPI- and App-Bound-
# Encryption-protected: they restore byte-identical and completely non-functional on any
# other machine or SID. They are worth keeping for a same-machine rollback and worth
# nothing for the move to the cloud desktop. Browser sessions do not survive that move --
# Bitwarden plus `gh auth login` is the real recovery path. Do not let their presence in
# the snapshot create a false sense of recoverability.
#
# `Extensions/` drops extension CODE (re-downloaded from the Web Store). Extension DATA
# survives via Local Extension Settings / Extension State / Storage/ext. Check
# chrome://extensions for anything sideloaded before trusting that split.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
